From: mecanum-robot <user@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] add missing #include <pthread.h> for GCC 13

log_module.cpp calls pthread_mutex_init/lock/unlock but never includes
<pthread.h>. On older GCC this resolved transitively; GCC 13 (the
ros:jazzy-ros-base image's compiler) no longer pulls it in, so the
build fails with "'pthread_mutex_lock' was not declared in this scope".

The include goes inside the existing LINUX branch so the Windows
(#ifndef LINUX, <comutil.h>) path is untouched.

Pinned to upstream commit bf668a8, applied as a local patch by
docker/apply-patches.sh before colcon build. Generated with `git diff`
against that commit so the context matches byte-for-byte.

diff --git a/ldlidar_driver/src/logger/log_module.cpp b/ldlidar_driver/src/logger/log_module.cpp
index 61369e0..a365425 100644
--- a/ldlidar_driver/src/logger/log_module.cpp
+++ b/ldlidar_driver/src/logger/log_module.cpp
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@
 #pragma comment(lib, "comsuppw.lib")
 #else
 #include <stdlib.h>
+#include <pthread.h>
 #endif
 
 //使用vswprintf会出现奔溃的情况如果，传入数据大于 VA_PARAMETER_MAX 就会出现崩溃
